{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5963,
  "title": "Render with createRoot() in renderWebChat() when ReactDOM.render() is not available",
  "body": "> Related to #5552 and #5850.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Added\n\n- `renderWebChat()`: added support of a root from `createRoot()` for React 19, related to [#5552](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/issues/5552) and [#5850](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/issues/5850), in PR [#5963](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5963), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\n`renderWebChat()` called `ReactDOM.render()`, which React 19 removed. It now also takes a root from `createRoot()` instead of the element; an element on React 19 throws, asking for `createRoot(element)`.\n\n## Design\n\n- Web Chat never imports `react-dom/client` (npm bundlers fail on it with React 16 and 17): the host creates the root.\n- DOM containers are checked first (Lit elements have `render()`); React 16 to 18 keep `ReactDOM.render()`, synchronously.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `renderWebChat.tsx`: element or root, typed; `renderWebChat.spec.tsx`: element, fragment, root, React 19 error\n- `isomorphic-react-dom`: bundled React DOM loads only without `window.ReactDOM` (crashed with React 19)\n- `react19/renderWebChat.{iife,esm}.html`: element throws; snapshot 1 root, 2 same root shows the send box\n- `react19/renderWebChat.{root,customElement}.react18.esm.html`: root; custom element with `render()`; snapshot 1\n- `HOSTING.md`: React 19 passes `createRoot(element)`\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [x] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
